.TH GETCORE 2
.SH NAME
getcore \- core number and role
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <u.h>
.br
.B #include <libc.h>
.PP
.B
int	getcore(int *rolep)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Getcore
returns the number of the processor the process runs on and, if
.I rolep
is not nil, sets
.BI * rolep
to its role, one of
.B NIXTC
(time-sharing core),
.B NIXAC
(application core, see
.IR execac (2))
and
.B NIXKC
(kernel core).
It reads them from the
.B Tos
structure (see
.IR exec (2)),
which the kernel updates each time the process leaves it,
and makes no system call.
On a time-sharing core the number may be stale: the process may
have moved since.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/libc/9sys/getcore.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR execac (2),
.IR cons (3)
